  summary: "Under Haile Selassie the imperial state reached its peak of centralization through military, police and intelligence instruments, governor-generals and the 1955 constitution, but it generated continuous opposition. Patriot plots, the failed coup of the Neway brothers in 1960, the Woyane, Bale and Gojjam peasant rebellions, the Eritrean armed struggle after 1961 and the ban on Mecha-Tulama, together with a radicalized student movement crying Land to the Tiller, steadily eroded absolutist rule and prepared the crisis of 1974.",
