      given: "The aim was to move 1.5 million people from the drought-prone north to fertile south and south-west lands; the outcome included broken families, deaths from malaria and sleeping sickness, and about 100,000 dead under the ill-planned program.",
      formula: "Historical skill: evaluating a policy by comparing goals with outcomes.",
