      given: "On 23 September 1976 the EPRP tried to kill Colonel Mengistu; during the summer of 1976 Mengistu had liquidated rivals such as Major Sisay Habte and Major Kiros Alamayahu; on 3 February 1977 Colonel Daniel Asfaw arrested General Teferi Benti and six leading PMAC members, who were all executed; in November 1977 Atnafu Abate was eliminated.",
      formula: "Historical skill: constructing a chain of causation from individual power struggles to regime change.",
      substitution: "Track rivals inside the PMAC removed in 1976, then the coup victims of February 1977, then the last rival in November 1977.",
      calculation: "With Benti dead and Atnafu gone, no credible challenger remained inside the ruling body, so the coup of February 1977 made Mengistu the sole ruler.",
